  "slug": "cosmological-order-phase-transitions-5f33",
  "summary": "Five preprints refine early-universe modeling, from nonlinear-gravity phase transitions to GW source models, with DESI DR2 constraints on inhomogeneity-driven acceleration.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is replacing simplified assumptions with more complete dynamics in cosmological modeling. One preprint simulates a first-order phase transition with full nonlinear general relativity (BSSN), reporting a gravitational wave peak amplitude of about 5e-11. Another models GW spectra from slowly evolving sources (turbulence, sound waves, bubble collisions) using constant-in-time and coherent-decay prescriptions. Warm inflation work shows shear viscosity in the radiation bath sources stochastic vector perturbations through fluctuating hydrodynamics. The neutrino self-interaction paper argues renormalizable theories imply resonant mediator behavior that modifies the Boltzmann hierarchy and the CMB ΔN_eff treatment. The late-time paper uses DESI DR2 BAO and SNe Ia to constrain Misner-Sharp mass in an exact GR solution where inhomogeneities induce acceleration. These are heterogeneous in epoch but share a focus on dynamics beyond standard approximations.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
